 The BFD 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 SpaceX inked an $8 billion deal to acquire a nationwide low-band spectrum portfolio from Grain Management on Thursday, per the WSJ .

 Why it's the BFD: AT&amp;T, Verizon, and T-Mobile shed some $36 billion in combined market cap on the news.

 SpaceX gained 3% — or $67 billion in pre-market trading.

 Between the lines: Buying these licenses allows it to reach areas that satellite currently struggles to do, like the inside of buildings.

 The bottom line: The spectrum could serve SpaceX's stated ambition of moving its Starlink satellite service beyond broadband into the wireless market to compete with the likes of AT&amp;T and Verizon." — WSJ 

